geoui.api:
OV.SceneDefs.geoscape({G}) — isScreen:true. Builds a DOM root `.geo.passthru` in #hud (right side panel, globe tools, selection card, top banner, central layer for popups/dialogs, first-visit hint). Draws OV.GlobeRender with view.cx shifted left of the panel. Persists camera/speed/radar in G.ui.geo and the intro flag in G.ui.geoIntro (UI-owned).

OV.GeoUI = {
  open(G)                                 OV.Game.G = G; OV.Scenes.set('geoscape', {G}) → scene
  centreOn(G, {lon,lat}|{kind,id}, zoom?) animates the open Geoscape camera; with no scene open, stores the position in G.ui.geo → bool
  intercept(G, ufoId?)                    opens the intercept flow (target preselected when given) → bool
  current() → {t, funds, view:{lon,lat,zoom,mode,selection}, speed 0..5, paused, popup:type|null, dialog:'intercept'|'funding'|'bases'|null, mode, draws, blocked, modal, queue:[types], waiting, fallbackDf, perf} | null   (QA/debug)
  setSpeed(i) ; togglePause() ; select({kind,id}|null)
  model = { pure, Node-tested: runClock(G, st{speed,paused,acc}, dt, handle(evs), opts?) → {steps,ticks,stopped,reason} (contract §6.3), REACT {eventType → 'popup'|'toast'|'scene'|'action'|'debug'|'none'}, classify(ev), MERGE, toastFor(G, type, evs) → {text, kind}, craftsFor(G, baseId|null, target|null) → [{craftId, baseId, ok, reason, warn, eta:{nm,h}}], targetsFor(G, craftId) → [{ref|'home', ok, reason, warn, eta}], launchState(G, craft), ufoRows/craftRows/baseRows/siteRows/alienBaseRows/cityRows(G, obj) → [[labelKey, value, {bar,tone}?]], ufoName, ufoTitle, craftName, baseName, cityName, countryName, placeName(lon,lat), targetName(G, ref), craftStatusKey, weaponsText, etaHours, fundingRows(G), fmtDur, fmtNm, fmtKn, fmtLL, compass, prodName, itemName, researchName, reasonText, warnText, textKeys(), WORLD_REASONS, WORLD_WARNS, MISSION_REASONS, ufoVisible }
}

Keys: 1–6 speeds; P / Space pause; I intercept (uses the selected UFO as target if one is selected); B bases; U Ufopédia; F funding; S save; Esc closes the innermost popup/dialog/target mode, otherwise opens options; C centre on selection; H centre on base; R radar circles; Tab / Shift+Tab cycle through UFOs, sites and airborne crafts; arrows rotate continuously; + / − zoom one level (animated). Card shortcuts: E send team, D new destination, M start mission. Popup buttons show their own keys; Enter = default button, Esc = dismiss.

Pointer: drag rotates with fling; two-finger scroll / 'pan' rotates; pinch / ctrl+wheel zoom anchored at the cursor; mouse-wheel notch zooms one level; click selects (repeat clicks cycle through stacked markers); double-click or Option-click centres; secondary (right / ctrl+click / long-press) centres, or cancels target mode.

Cross-module calls (all feature-detected):
OV.DogfightUI.open(G) (fallback: built-in auto-resolving interception popup ticking OV.Dogfight.tick, max 8 ticks/frame);
OV.BaseUI.open(G, baseId, tab) with tabs research / production / facilities / soldiers / personnel / crafts / stores;
OV.Ufopaedia.open(G, article);
OV.CampaignUI.launchMission(G, siteRef, craftId) (fallback: Campaign.startMission → Battle.create → push 'battlescape' with onExit → finishMission → 'debrief' → onDone → GeoUI.open / CampaignUI.victory / gameOver);
OV.CampaignUI.monthReport(G, report), gameOver(G, reason), victory(G), saveDialog(G), autosave(G) — each with a fallback (popup, or OV.Save.save('auto'|'1', G, null, {label}));
OV.Screens.openOptions().

i18n: all player text uses geo.* keys in js/i18n/pt-PT.geoui.js. This includes geo.err.<World reason>, geo.warn.<warn>, geo.err.mission.<campaign.err reason>, geo.save.err.<busy|quota|unavailable|slot>, and texts for every popup and toast event type.

geoui.summary:
The Geoscape screen is done and wired to the real campaign. `qa/geo_check.mjs` runs the whole requested flow in Chromium and passes all 36 checks, with no console errors and no missing text keys. The Node suite is green with `--strict --i18n`: 563 passed, 0 failed. My new test file accounts for 8 of those.

**What the player gets**
- **Globe:** full-screen globe from OV.GlobeRender with drag + fling, two-finger rotate, pinch / ctrl+wheel / +− zoom through the 6 levels with animation, double-click / Option-click / right-click to centre, and continuous arrow-key rotation.
- **Clock:** the contract's time loop (80 ms steps, 720-tick chunks, 12 ms frame budget, no time debt). Six speeds on keys 1–6, P/Space pause. Any stopping event drops to 5 s and freezes time while its popup, a dialog, target mode or another scene is open. Measured game seconds per 1.2 s of real time match the speed table (75 / 900 / 4 500 / ~27 000 / ~54 000 s, then 1 dia stops at the first detection).
- **Right panel:** date and time («1 jan 1999 · 12:05»), funds, pause and speed buttons, Interceptar / Bases / Ufopédia / Financiamento / Gravar / Opções, and live lists of detected UFOs, sites (terror + alien bases) and airborne crafts with click-to-centre.
- **Selection cards:**
  - UFO: type and race only with hyper-wave, size, altitude, heading, speed, place.
  - Craft: status, destination, ETA, fuel and hull bars, weapons, crew, with Regressar / Patrulhar / Novo destino / Iniciar missão.
  - Base: radars, crafts with a Lançar button each. Terror site with time left; alien base.
- **Interception:** base → craft → target (UFO / site / alien base / return home / any point picked on the globe). Every row shows live World.canOrder validity, refusal reasons and the noWeapons / tooSlow / tooFar warnings in pt-PT, with ETA and distance. Target mode shows a dashed path and a banner that validates whatever is under the cursor.
- **Events:** every type in OV.Campaign.EVENTS has a reaction (a test enforces this). Stopping events become one-at-a-time popups with actions; similar popups (facility / production / delivery) merge; the rest become grouped toasts. The terror popup is red with a siren and switches music to the terror mood while a site exists. The camera centres the event's object in the free area beside the popup so it is never hidden. Monthly report, autosave and game end go to CampaignUI.

**QA run** (`qa/geo_check.mjs`; a full run takes about 5 minutes):
- campaign created at Lisbon, Medi-Kit research started through OV.BaseSim;
- all six speeds, then a UFO detection;
- an Interceptor launched from the popup, the dogfight overlay in aggressive mode, «OVNI abatido»;
- «Enviar equipa» with the Skyranger, «Iniciar missão?», and the campaign briefing opening;
- research-done and production-done popups (Medi-Kit production started through OV.BaseSim);
- the funding panel and the base card;
- the February month report through CampaignUI.

I reviewed the screenshots over six QA rounds and fixed what they showed:
- the root element was swallowing all globe input (a CSS specificity problem);
- popups covered the object they were about;
- a literal "null" appeared in popups;
- labels were cut off at 1024 and 1280 px;
- the hint overlapped the card;
- the craft card showed two primary buttons;
- some pt-PT wording around base and place names, and the race name in the terror popup.

**Frame rate (not met here):** this container has no GPU. At 1440×900 @2× in this container, rotating the globe runs at 6.7–11 fps, and a globe draw while moving costs 20–96 ms of JS depending on CPU load. Idle frames are about 0.2 ms. The globe redraws at most 10 Hz while time runs and only when something changes when paused. The ≥ 50 fps target needs checking on a real Mac.

